// endpoint_await_agent_by_vendor_task.proto — AwaitAgentByVendorTask: WHICH
// AGENT a vendor task locator names, and what it was commissioned with,
// answered once the record holds both.
//
// WHY A WAIT. A subagent spawned BY A SUBAGENT (a nested spawn) starts from a
// call in its spawner's own transcript, which only the sidecar reads; the
// vendor announces the nested task on the shim's stream, often before the
// sidecar has read either half (2026-11-18: asked 0.66s before the pickup, and
// answered not_found). GetAgentByVendorTask answers the record as it stands, so
// its answer depended on which of the two came first. This one answers only
// once the pairing and the agent's start are both on record, so their order
// cannot matter.
//
// THE CALLER BOUNDS IT. The wait has no bound of its own: it ends when the
// record answers, when the caller's deadline or cancellation ends the call
// (a transport error the caller records), or when the store shuts down
// (UNAVAILABLE).
//
// SCOPED LIKE GetAgentByVendorTask: the answer is confined to the caller's
// lineage.

